grow - extend a partition and its filesystem over free space

  grow usb0p3

The system image gives /home 16 MiB whatever the card's size. grow extends
the partition over free space after it, then the filesystem over the
partition.

`disk` shows which volume is mounted at /home: usb0p3 when the 701 boots
from SD. Unmount it first.

A larger allocation table moves the data area forward. Cluster numbers do
not change.

A power cut during the move destroys the volume. Copy important files off
first.

Refused on a mounted volume, a filesystem already filling its partition,
or one that would need a wider FAT than it has.
